  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><em>Category: Seen Gods</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Primarily Practiced in: Zahnheim, North Rodda</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Espirian Domains: The Heavens (Valtal), The Hells (Obscurum)</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">The Armsman is a hero of glory, seeing ever greater heights and fame as they exceed their skills. Warriors, gladiators and heroes face the world and see every new weapon, skill or course as a challenge to be mastered. Monivol embodies his seat by being a patron deity that is often seen by those who attend the games held at the Lakheronis Arena, watching from Mount Oropedus and choosing contestants to receive his blessing – and seeing if the underdog rises to the challenge. He appears as a brown-furred garou, wielding a bejeweled sword said to have been crafted and emblazoned with the riches he amassed when his name is invoked to complete a contest or earn a hard-earned victory.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Title</strong> The Armsman</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Edicts</strong> Engage in competition, learn and master new skills, wield new weapons of war</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Anathema</strong> Take shortcuts to victory, leave weapons and skills to rust</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> Competition, Weaponry, Challenges</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> A closed fist clutching a crown</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Animal</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> Anteater</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Colors</strong></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> Silver and Brown</span></p>"
    },
